#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:10
msgid ""
"This Masterclass is an introduction to the use of the environment similarity"
" CV available in PLUMED to the calculation of liquid-solid free energy "
"differences (chemical potentials)."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass では PLUMED の Environment Similarity CV "
"を使い、液固の自由エネルギー差（Chemical Potential）を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:12
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:14
msgid "The objectives of this Masterclass are:"
msgstr "この Masterclass の到達目標は次のとおりである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:15
msgid ""
"Learn to define reference environments for a crystal structure and choose "
"appropriate parameters"
msgstr "結晶構造の参照 Environment と適切なパラメータを定義する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid ""
"Learn how to run **bulk interconversion** simulations in which the bulk "
"liquid and the bulk solid are reversibly interconverted"
msgstr "Bulk の液体と固体を可逆に変換する **Bulk Interconversion** を実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:17
msgid ""
"Learn how to run **biased coexistence** simulations (similar to interface "
"pinning)"
msgstr "Interface Pinning に似た **Biased Coexistence** を実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:18
msgid "Learn how to perform **thermodynamic integration** along isobars"
msgstr "Isobars に沿って **Thermodynamic Integration** を行う方法を学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:19
msgid "Understand the importance of finite size effects"
msgstr "Finite-size Effects の重要性を理解する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:20
msgid "Understand the advantages and limitations of each method"
msgstr "各手法の利点と限界を理解する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:21
msgid "Understand how these methods complement each other"
msgstr "これらの手法が互いにどう補い合うかを理解する。"

