msgid ""
"The definition above is only useful for Bravais lattices since these have a "
"single, unique atomic environment. The kernel can be generalized to crystal "
"structures described as a lattice with a basis of more than one atom. As "
"discussed above, in this case there is more than one type of environment. We"
" consider the case of $M$ environments $X = \\chi_1,\\chi_2,...,\\chi_M$ and"
" we define the kernel through a best match strategy:"
msgstr ""
"この定義は原子 Environment が1種類の Bravais Lattice 用ですが、Basis が複数原子の結晶にも一般化できます。$M$ "
"Environment $X = \\chi_1,\\chi_2,...,\\chi_M$ に対し Best Match で、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:84
msgid ""
"For a large enough $\\lambda$ this expression will select the largest "
"$\\tilde{k}_{\\chi_l}(\\chi)$ with $\\chi_l\\in X$."
msgstr "十分大きな $\\lambda$ は、$\\chi_l\\in X$ の最大 $\\tilde{k}_{\\chi_l}(\\chi)$ を選びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:86
msgid ""
"$\\tilde{k}_X(\\chi)$ is a per-atom quantity and we will have to compute "
"global functions of these quantities, for instance, the mean or the number "
"of atoms with at $\\tilde{k}_X(\\chi)$ larger than some value."
msgstr ""
"$\\tilde{k}_X(\\chi)$ は各原子の量なので、平均や $\\tilde{k}_X(\\chi)$ "
"が閾値を超える数などの全体量を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:88
msgid "The system: Sodium as the alanine dipeptide of solids"
msgstr "対象系：固体における Alanine Dipeptide に相当する Sodium"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:90
msgid ""
"Alanine dipeptide is the prototypical system on which enhanced sampling "
"methods are tested (and sometimes benchmarked) on. The reasons behind this "
"choice is that alanine dipeptide is a small and relatively simple molecule "
"that nonetheless captures well the phenomenon of conformational isomerism "
"with relatively large free energy barriers. I argue that a similar system in"
" the context of materials is sodium. It crystallizes in the bcc structure "
"which is one of the simplest crystal structures. Also, it does not show the "
"competition between fcc and hcp structures typical of systems that "
"crystallize in these two compact structures. This fact greatly simplifies "
"the task of characterizing the structure: all that we can see is liquid or "
"bcc environments. We will use an embedded atom model (EAM) for sodium that "
"is described in [this "
"paper](https://aip.scitation.org/doi/full/10.1063/1.4916741). The melting "
"temperature is supposed to be 366 K. Let's see if we can reproduce that "
"result."
msgstr ""
"Alanine Dipeptide は小さく単純ながら大きな Barrier の Isomerism を捉え、Enhanced Sampling "
"の典型テスト系です。材料で同様なのが Sodium だと考えます。単純な bcc に結晶化し、Compact な fcc/hcp "
"間競合もないため、液体か bcc "
"のみを区別できます。[この論文](https://aip.scitation.org/doi/full/10.1063/1.4916741) の "
"Embedded Atom Model (EAM) を使い、報告融点366 K を再現できるか調べます。"

