#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:194
msgid "Exercise 2: Bulk interconversion"
msgstr "演習2：Bulk Interconversion"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:200
msgid ""
"We now move to the first method to calculate chemical potentials, the bulk "
"interconversion method. This method is based on simulating the reversible "
"interconversion of the liquid to the solid and calculating the difference in"
" chemical potential using:"
msgstr "まず Bulk Interconversion で可逆な固液変換を行い、Chemical Potential 差を次で求めます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:205
msgid ""
"with $Z_\\alpha$ and $Z_\\beta$ the partition functions restricted to each "
"phase. These are computed with the formulae,"
msgstr "$Z_\\alpha$、$Z_\\beta$ は各相に制限した Partition Function で、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:212
msgid ""
"assuming that the collective variable $s$ can separate well the phases at "
"threshold $s^*$. The ratio of the partition functions is easy to calculate "
"if we have a simulation in which both phases are visited, as we shall see "
"below."
msgstr "CV $s$ が閾値 $s^*$ で相をよく分けると仮定します。両相を訪れる MD なら比を容易に求められます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:215
msgid ""
"In a standard MD simulation we would only observe a single phase, and in "
"order to see interconversion we need to apply a bias potential. Here we will"
" use OPES to construct a bias potential as a function of the environment "
"similarity kernels. If you prefer to use METAD or VES, you can do so, "
"adapting the input accordingly."
msgstr ""
"通常 MD は一相しか見ないため、OPES で Kernel に BiasPotential を加えます。入力を変えて METAD・VES も使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:219
msgid ""
"The environment similarity kernel, which are per-atom quantities, can be "
"combined into a global quantity by evaluating how many have a value larger "
"than some threshold. In file ```2-bulk-"
"interconversion/250atoms/400K/plumed.dat``` we can see the input for a "
"simulation with 250 atoms at 400 K,"
msgstr ""
"Kernel の閾値超の原子数を全体量とします。```2-bulk-"
"interconversion/250atoms/400K/plumed.dat``` は250原子、400 K の例です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:232
msgid ""
"Here you see that we are calculating the MEAN and the number of atoms that "
"have a value of the kernel MORE_THAN something. Here, instead of having a "
"strict threshold at some value, we have a continuous and differentiable "
"switching function that is 0 below 0.38, 1 above 0.80, and changes smoothly "
"from 0 to 1 between these values. The values for D_0 and D_MAX have been "
"chosen based on the maxima of the distributions determined in the previous "
"exercise. Did you get those values right? I hope you did."
msgstr ""
"MEAN と MORE_THAN の数を求めます。厳密な閾値でなく、0.38未満で0、0.80超で1、その間を滑らかに変わる微分可能な "
"Switching Function です。D_0・D_MAX は前の分布 Peak から決めました。同じ値になりましたか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:236
msgid "The input for OPES is very simple,"
msgstr "OPES の入力は非常に単純である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:240
msgid ""
"and uses the morethan value described above as CV. We estimate a barrier of "
"less than 100 kJ/mol and that's the rationale behind the choice of BARRIER. "
"If you are using well tempered METAD you might want to use a biasfactor of "
"around 40. The other keywords are fairly standard."
msgstr ""
"morethan を CV にします。Barrier は100 kJ/mol 未満と見積もり、BARRIER を選びました。Well-tempered "
"METAD なら Bias Factor 約40を試せます。ほかは標準的です。"

